  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Flood Response in Mbale</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Elgon region is one of the regions in Uganda prone to recurrent disasters associated with heavy rainfall such as landslides and floods given its geographical set up aligned in three zones. The highland zone is prone to landslides and mass wasting of soils, hailstorms, falling boulders, deep cracks while the mid highland zone is also at risk and experiences the impacts of the highland disasterwith falling debris and boulders. In both cases, communities experience , loss of lives, loss of crops and livestock, as well as destruction of houses and  infrastructure such as water supply systems, sanitation facilities, schools, health facilities, churches  and road networks. The wide spread  flooding leads to risks of water borne diseases , crop pest and animaldiseases.
During the period July to October 2022 , the heavy rains received cross the region affected a number of districts, with  Mbale, Sironko, Bulambuli, Bududa and Mbale City being the most severely affected; live were lost  and property destroyed.</narrative>
  </description>
